{
  "analysis": "The JR/JALR fix helped but the VM is still stuck in a loop around fwrite/fread/fclose. The trace code wasn't fully removed. The key issue is that fwrite is called with null ptr/stream in a loop. I need to check vprintf_internal's NULL stream handling and understand the full call chain. Let me also check if syscalls are being reached at all.",
  "plan": "Inspect vprintf_internal source, fully remove trace code, add targeted syscall tracing, and check the full call chain from the beginning. Then fix the root cause.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '2500,2560p' /tmp/stdlib_lines.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n \"trace\\|instCount <\" /app/vm.js | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'\n# Fully remove all trace code and add clean syscall tracing\nsrc=open('/app/vm.js').read()\n# Remove any remaining trace lines\nimport re\nsrc=re.sub(r'\\n\\s*if \\(this\\.instCount.*?console\\.error\\(`\\[trace\\].*?`\\);\\n', '\\n', src)\nsrc=re.sub(r'\\n\\s*if \\(\\(pc.*?console\\.error\\(`\\[trace\\].*?`\\);\\n', '\\n', src)\n# Add clean syscall tracing at the start of syscall()\nsrc=src.replace('    const a5 = this.r[9] >>> 0;\\n    let ret = 0;', '    const a5 = this.r[9] >>> 0;\\n    if (this.instCount < 500000) console.error(`[syscall] v0=${v0} a0=${a0} a1=${a1} a2=${a2} pc=${this.pc.toString(16)} inst=${this.instCount}`);\\n    let ret = 0;')\nopen('/app/vm.js','w').write(src)\nPY\nnode -c /app/vm.js\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f /tmp/frame.bmp /tmp/vm_out.txt; timeout 15 node /app/vm.js > /tmp/vm_out.txt 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\"; wc -l /tmp/vm_out.txt; head -60 /tmp/vm_out.txt; echo '...'; tail -10 /tmp/vm_out.txt; ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 17.0
    }
  ]
